From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:54:53 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: reserve a ramoops region on the FRITZ!Box 7560

The board has no JTAG. The serial console is the only post-mortem channel
there is, which means a wedge nobody is watching leaves nothing behind at
all. Reserve 1 MiB for pstore's ram backend so the tail of the kernel log
survives into the next boot.

The address is picked by three constraints rather than convenience. We
do not build CONFIG_EVA, so the kernel loads at physical 0x20020000 and
the vendor's own ramoops region -- 4 MiB at 0x20100000, which works for
them only because they do build CONFIG_EVA and load at 0x20500000 -- is
inside our image. The region also has to stay low enough that a recovery
image staged in RAM cannot overwrite the record being diagnosed. That
leaves the gap immediately below 0x23800000.

The zone split is lopsided towards the console on purpose. A watchdog
bite is not an oops, so nothing calls kmsg_dump and the dmesg zones only
ever fill on a real panic -- and each one stores at most
PSTORE_DEFAULT_KMSG_BYTES of a single part, so sizing them generously
reserves space that can never be used. The console zone is the only thing
that captures a silent wedge, which is precisely the case this
reservation exists for.

mem-type = <1> maps the region uncached, because a record has to be in
DRAM rather than a dirty cache line when the watchdog pulls the reset and
nothing flushes on that path. Not no-map: all that is wanted is for the
allocator to keep off the region, which memblock_reserve does, whereas
no-map asks the architecture to leave the range out of its own mapping
for no benefit here.

Whether the contents survive the RCU warm reset at all is not something
the vendor sources answer, and it is what the hardware test is for.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi
index cf26ea178c63..7108b3415d75 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi
@@ -82,6 +82,14 @@ reserved-memory {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
 		ranges;
+
+		ramoops@23700000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x23700000 0x100000>;
+			record-size = <0x4000>;
+			console-size = <0x80000>;
+			mem-type = <1>;
+		};
 	};
 };
 
